---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactLinks from '../components/ContactLinks.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { earlier } from '../data/content';
---
<Base title="About" description="Avnish Singh, final-year computer science student at Babu Banarasi Das University, Lucknow. Looking for AI/ML engineering internships and entry-level roles.">
  <p class="page-note hand">Lucknow, graduating May 2027.</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

  <p>
    I'm Avnish Singh, a final-year B.Tech student in Computer Science and Engineering at {site.school} in Lucknow,
    graduating in {site.graduation}.
  </p>
  <p>
    My projects keep coming back to one habit: decide the metric and the bar before running the experiment, and keep the
    result when it goes against me. In OmitBench that meant publishing that my own detector lost, and retiring two detectors
    that missed a bar I had set in advance.
  </p>
  <p>
    I build with AI coding assistants, mainly Claude and Copilot, and I review what they write for architecture as well as
    syntax. Every session ends with the test output pasted back, because "done" from an assistant is a claim, not a result.
  </p>

  <h2>What I'm looking for</h2>
  <p>
    ML engineering work where models have to survive contact with production. Internships and entry-level roles, in India,
    remote, Japan, Europe, the US or Canada. I'm eligible to work in India and open to relocation.
  </p>
  <ContactLinks />

  <h2>Education</h2>
  <p>B.Tech, Computer Science and Engineering, {site.school}, Lucknow. 2023 to 2027, CGPA 7.39 out of 10.</p>

  <h2>Outside work</h2>
  <p>
    I speak Hindi and English, and I've just started learning Japanese, so I'm a beginner, below JLPT N5.
    I write poetry under the pen name Anand Avnish, and I play chess. I won my college tournament in 2025.
  </p>

  <h2>Earlier projects</h2>
  <ul class="earlier">
    {earlier.map((p) => (
      <li><a href={p.href}>{p.title}</a>. {p.summary}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-note {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    color: var(--yellow);
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
    transform-origin: left;
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .page-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 3.1rem);
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.024em;
    font-weight: 750;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 2.9rem 0 0.8rem;
  }
  .earlier {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .earlier li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .earlier li::marker {
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }
</style>
